# Build context is ./build (docs/hosting.md 3.5). Three files -- Dockerfile, modules.txt,
# entrypoint.sh -- plus modules/, which holds modules versioned in this repo rather than pinned in
# modules.txt. Nothing here may exclude modules/ or any part of it: the Dockerfile COPYs it whole,
# INCLUDING each module's data/sql/**, which is how its migrations reach DBUpdater at runtime.
# `build/cache/` is gitignored at the repo root for a local ccache directory -- if one exists
# it must not be shipped to the daemon as build context, and it must not bust the cache key of
# every layer by changing on each run.
cache/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Byte-compiled Python from the module generators under modules/*/tools/. Excluded for the layer
# cache, not for size: `COPY modules/ /src/modules/` sits directly above the compile, so any
# change under build/modules/ invalidates it -- and running a generator rewrites .pyc timestamps
# even when the .py is untouched. Left in, an unrelated `dkspells.py --help` would cost a full
# AzerothCore rebuild.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
